      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "d_04",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "04-Configuration.md",
      "x": 1860,
      "y": -1420,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_ui",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "INTERFACE",
      "x": -1660,
      "y": -260,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 1210,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "browser",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Browser**  \u00b7  `frontend/index.html`\n\nQuestion box \u00b7 depth selector (rounds 1\u20134)\nCards: Source Retrieval, Evidence Extraction,\nResearch Plan, Searches, Evidence Check,\nWhere Sources Disagree, status banner, report\n\nLive progress via SSE; never a blank wait",
      "x": -1620,
      "y": -220,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 250,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "fe_js",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`app.js`** 693 \u00b7 **`markdown.js`** 325 \u00b7 **`style.css`** 743\n\n`app.js` reads `response.body` as a stream, splits\n`\\n\\n`, parses `data:` frames.\n\n`markdown.js` escapes everything *then* renders.\nAutolinks extracted before escaping so reference\nURLs stay clickable. `[n]` \u2192 `#ref-n` anchors.\nReferences \u2192 ONE `<ol>` (else each restarts at 1).",
      "x": -1620,
      "y": 70,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "api",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`backend/main.py`** 85\n\n`GET /api/research?q=&rounds=` \u2014 SSE, rounds\nclamped 1\u20134, every frame `data: {json}\\n\\n`\n`GET /api/report/download` \u2014 attachment\n`GET /api/report/markdown` \u2014 JSON\n\nMounts `/` (frontend) and `/exports`",
      "x": -1620,
      "y": 390,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "sse",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`researcher.py`** 103\n\nLangGraph node updates \u2192 SSE events.\nThe only module that imports `graph.py`.\n\n`status` emitted *before* `report` so the UI can\nrender state before a 100 KB body arrives.",
      "x": -1620,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_orch",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "ORCHESTRATION",
      "x": -972,
      "y": -60,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 790,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "graph",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`graph.py`** 446 \u2014 `CompiledStateGraph`\n\n8 nodes \u00b7 4 conditional edges\n**`Send`** fan-out \u2192 parallel workers\n**`operator.add`** reducers \u2192 safe concurrent merge\n`astream(stream_mode=\"updates\")` \u2192 SSE\n\n\u26a0 Orchestration only. All research logic is plain\nPython *inside* nodes.",
      "x": -932,
      "y": -20,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 330,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "state",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`State`** \u2014 `TypedDict(total=False)`\n\nReducer keys (merge, not overwrite):\n`raw` \u00b7 `log` \u00b7 `notes`\n\nAccumulate across rounds:\n`retrieval_index` (url \u2192 best grade, never re-fetch)\n`documents_by_url` \u00b7 `extracted`\n\nPer-run objects: `budget` (`CallBudget`) \u00b7\n`fetcher` (fetch budget is per run)",
      "x": -932,
      "y": 350,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_pipe",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "PIPELINE NODES  (LangGraph, left \u2192 right)",
      "x": -284,
      "y": -300,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 2760,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "n_planner",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`planner`** \u00b7 LLM \u00d71\n\nQuestion \u2192 3\u20135 sub-questions, each with\nweb / news / scholar / github searches.\nTypical run: 7 searches.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": -260,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 210
    },
    {
      "id": "n_sworker",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`search_worker`** \u00b7 no LLM\n\n**Fanned out in parallel via `Send`.**\nMeasured peak concurrency **6** (asyncio_0\u20265,\nstart within 11 ms) \u2192 **1.4 s** wall vs 4.9 s\nsequential = **3.5\u00d7 faster**.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": -20,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 250,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "n_collect",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`collect`** \u00b7 no LLM\n\nDedupe by normalised URL (`www.`, trailing\nslash folded), drop URL-less rows, flag\n\u22653 years as `stale`.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": 250,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 200
    },
    {
      "id": "n_retrieve",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`retrieve`** \u00b7 no LLM\n\nSkip URLs already read \u2192 fetch \u2192 grade \u2192 fold\ninto `retrieval_index` \u2192 mine references \u2192\nre-chunk the union.\n\n`_aggregate_retrieval()` derives **all** counters\nfrom that one index, so `attempted == full +\npartial + metadata_only + failed` always holds.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "n_chunker",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`chunker`** \u00b7 no LLM\n\nStructure-aware split. Headings \u2192 section path\n(`Performance > UI frame rate`), PDF `\\f` \u2192 page\nnumbers. Never truncates a document whole.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": 830,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 220
    },
    {
      "id": "n_relevance",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`relevance`** \u00b7 no LLM\n\nIDF-weighted overlap \u00b7 boost dimension coverage\nand quantitative content \u00b7 penalise boilerplate\n\u00b7 `diversify()` round-robin so one verbose\ndocument cannot flood the batch.\n\nAlso extracts `targets` and `dimensions` from the\nquestion \u2014 these decide the report's sections.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": 1080,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 280
    },
    {
      "id": "n_extract",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`extract`** \u00b7 LLM **batched**\n\nChunks packed to 13k chars per call; one call\nyields every finding those chunks support.\n\nPasses every record through the two guards \u2192\n`evidence.py` \u2192 `quote_is_supported()`.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": 1390,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 230,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "n_gap",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`gap_check`** \u00b7 LLM \u00d71\n\nIs there a *specific* gap worth another round?\n`round >= max_rounds` stops the loop \u2014 **our**\nbound, not LangGraph's `recursion_limit`.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": 1650,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 210
    },
    {
      "id": "n_contra",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`contradiction_check`** \u00b7 LLM batched\n\nGenuine disagreements between findings.\nInstructed to separate real conflicts from\ndifferences explained by date, workload or scope.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": 1890,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 210
    },
    {
      "id": "n_synth",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`synthesizer`** \u00b7 LLM ~14\n\n`assign_references()` runs **before any model\ncall** \u2192 a fabricated citation has no number to\nreference. Then one call per section, each given\nonly its own evidence slice.\n\nEmits `ReportResult(markdown, status,\nmissing_sections)` and writes the export.",
      "x": -244,
      "y": 2130,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 290,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_modA",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "RETRIEVAL & EVIDENCE MODULES",
      "x": 384,
      "y": -300,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 2790,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "m_planner",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`planner.py`** 19\n\nOne `ask()` \u2192 JSON sub-questions. Rejects\ninvalid shapes rather than repairing them;\nfilters to known sources, non-empty queries.",
      "x": 424,
      "y": -260,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 200
    },
    {
      "id": "m_searcher",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`searcher.py`** 139\n\n`search(source, query, n)` \u2192 SerpApi.\n`web`\u2192google \u00b7 `news`\u2192google_news \u00b7\n`scholar`\u2192google_scholar \u00b7\n`github`\u2192google + `site:github.com`\n\nNormalises to `{title,url,snippet,date,type,query}`.\nOptional disk cache \u00b7 full mock mode.",
      "x": 424,
      "y": -30,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 290
    },
    {
      "id": "m_collector",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`collector.py`** 60\n\nDedupe \u00b7 freshness flag \u00b7 `context(limit=40)`\nrenders the numbered block a model sees.\n`year_of()` parses loose date strings.",
      "x": 424,
      "y": 290,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 180
    },
    {
      "id": "m_fetch",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`fetch.py`** 724\n\n**5 parallel parse branches:**\n\u2022 PDF \u2192 `pypdf`, per page, `\\f` markers\n\u2022 arXiv \u2192 arXiv API (title/authors/date/DOI)\n\u2022 GitHub \u2192 REST API (stars/licence/topics) + README\n\u2022 HTML \u2192 `lxml`, article container only\n\u2022 plain / md / json \u2192 verbatim\n\n**Graded:** `full` / `partial` / `metadata_only` /\n`failed`. Honours robots.txt; 429/5xx retried\nonce. `_structured_text()` preserves headings,\ntables and code indentation.",
      "x": 424,
      "y": 500,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 470,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "m_chunker",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`chunker.py`** 262\n\n`chunk_document()` groups blocks to\n`CHUNK_TARGET_CHARS`, hard-caps at\n`CHUNK_MAX_CHARS`, splits an oversized block on\nsentence boundaries, samples evenly when a doc\nexceeds `CHUNKS_PER_SOURCE`.\n\n`Chunk` carries `section`, `page`, `chunk_id`,\n`char_start`, `retrieval_status`, `doi`.",
      "x": 424,
      "y": 1000,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "m_relevance",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`relevance.py`** 231\n\n`rank()` IDF overlap \u00b7 `diversify()` per-source\ncap \u00b7 `targets()` / `dimensions()` string\nextraction.\n\nNo model calls anywhere in this file.",
      "x": 424,
      "y": 1330,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 230
    },
    {
      "id": "m_references",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`references.py`** 139\n\nBounded lead mining from outbound links and\nDOIs of documents actually read.\nCapped at `REFERENCES_MAX=6`, per-source 3,\n**depth 1**. Skips social / account-wall hosts.\n\nNo uncontrolled crawling.",
      "x": 424,
      "y": 1590,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 240
    },
    {
      "id": "m_evidence",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`evidence.py`** 270\n\nLeaf module. `Evidence` dataclass \u00b7\n`quote_is_supported()` sliding-window overlap \u00b7\n`dedupe()` \u00b7 `statistics()`.\n\n`usable_url` prefers **DOI over URL** so citations\nalways resolve to something canonical.",
      "x": 424,
      "y": 1860,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 290,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_modB",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "LLM, GUARDS & SYNTHESIS",
      "x": 1072,
      "y": -300,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 2250,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "m_llm",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`llm.py`** 611 \u2014 the only path to a model\n\nChain = `[role override, LLM_MODEL] + LLM_FALLBACKS`,\ndeduped, order preserved.\n\n**Retry policy**\n\u2022 rate limit (429) \u2192 advance, never same model\n\u2022 request-too-large \u2192 advance **+ learn ceiling**\n\u2022 transient 5xx \u2192 retry same model, 1/2/4 s + jitter\n\u2022 non-retryable (Auth/NotFound/BadRequest) \u2192 advance\n\u2022 programming errors \u2192 propagate, never swallowed\n\nPer-model cooldown table \u00b7 `CallBudget` \u00b7 mock mode.",
      "x": 1112,
      "y": -260,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 420,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "m_guards",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**The two anti-fabrication guards**\n\nRun deterministically *after* every extraction call.\nIn one real run these discarded **4 fabricated\ncitations**.\n\n**1** record names a `chunk_id` that was not in the\nbatch \u2192 *discarded*\n\n**2** quote not findable in its passage (\u226572% word\noverlap) and a number is involved \u2192 *discarded*\n\n`metadata_only` further forced to `weak`,\nconfidence \u2264 0.3, with the document marked **NOT read**.",
      "x": 1112,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 400,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "m_report",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`report.py`** 674\n\n`assign_references()` \u2014 url\u2192n, by strength, **before\nany model call** \u00b7 `render_references()` sequential\n1..N \u00b7 `_evidence_table()` deterministic \u00b7\n7 section prompts sharing one discipline block\n(cite the exact claim \u00b7 never invent a number \u00b7\nkeep conditions with numbers \u00b7 vendor claims are\ninterested parties \u00b7 say the evidence is insufficient).\n\n`classify_status()` \u2192 `completed` / `partial` / `failed`.",
      "x": 1112,
      "y": 640,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 400,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "m_prompts",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`report_prompts.py`** 13\n\nThe original single-call prompt, kept verbatim.\nUsed only by the no-evidence fallback path, so a\nsnippet-only run still produces a short summary\n(flagged `partial`, never passed off as deep).",
      "x": 1112,
      "y": 1350,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 200
    },
    {
      "id": "m_export",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`export.py`** 125\n\n`save()` \u2192 `exports/<slug>-<date>.md` with YAML\nfront matter recording what was actually read.\nRemembers the path per question so\n`/api/report/download` can serve it back.",
      "x": 1112,
      "y": 1080,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 240,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_ext",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "EXTERNAL",
      "x": 1760,
      "y": -300,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 1290,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "x_serp",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**SerpApi**\n\n`web`\u2192google \u00b7 `news`\u2192google_news\n`scholar`\u2192google_scholar\n`github`\u2192google + `site:` filter\n\n**~42 rows** from 7 queries",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": -260,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 220,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "x_docs",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**The open web**\n\nPDFs \u00b7 arXiv preprints \u00b7 GitHub READMEs \u00b7\nHTML articles \u00b7 official documentation\n\nA representative run: 67 attempted \u2192 **25 fetched**\n(24 full, 1 partial) \u2192 **64,796 words** \u2192 135 chunks\n\n\u26a0 **~\u2153 unreachable**: robots.txt disallows (Reddit,\nFacebook, LinkedIn), bot protection (Medium,\nIndeed), origin 429s. Kept as `metadata_only`.",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": -10,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 330,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "x_llm",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**LLM providers**\n\nGemini \u2192 OpenRouter \u2192 Cohere \u2192 Groq (last)\n\n**Groq free tier caps at 8,000 TPM.** Section\nprompts measured **8,500\u20139,800 tokens**, exceeding\nthe whole window on their own \u2014 one request can\nnever succeed there, whatever the wait.",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 290,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "x_quota",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Provider quotas**\n\nGemini daily quota (seen exhausted, ~18 h)\nGroq TPM ceiling\n\nMitigation: learned per-model **prompt ceilings** +\na 900 s oversized cooldown, so an oversized\nprompt is routed away instead of retried.",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_out",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "OUTPUT",
      "x": 2448,
      "y": 100,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 1330,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "o_events",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**SSE event stream**\n\n`plan` \u00b7 `results` \u00b7 `evidence` \u00b7 `retrieval`\n`analysis` \u00b7 `gap` \u00b7 `contradictions`\n**`status`** \u00b7 `report` \u00b7 `error` \u00b7 `done`\n\n`error` then `done` are always the last frames.",
      "x": 2488,
      "y": 140,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "o_status",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Completion state**\n\n`completed` \u00b7 `partial` \u00b7 `failed`\n\nSurfaced **four** ways:\n1. the `status` SSE event\n2. the `report` event's `status` field\n3. a banner inside the markdown itself\n4. frontend banner + card class\n\nA lost section can never read as a finished run.",
      "x": 2488,
      "y": 450,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "o_report",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Final report**\n\n11,000\u201314,000 words \u00b7 19\u201339 references\nsequential `1..N`, every number resolves to a\ncanonical, clickable URL\n\nSections: Executive Summary \u00b7 Scope and\nMethodology \u00b7 one per requested dimension \u00b7\nWhere the Evidence Conflicts \u00b7 Scenario Analysis \u00b7\nDecision Framework \u00b7 Evidence Quality and\nLimitations \u00b7 Conclusion \u00b7 Evidence by Source \u00b7\nReferences.",
      "x": 2488,
      "y": 800,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 380,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "o_file",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`exports/*.md`**\n\nDownloadable \u00b7 carries front matter and the\npartial banner, so a saved file is still honest\nwhen reopened weeks later.",
      "x": 2488,
      "y": 1210,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "g_cross",
      "type": "group",
      "label": "CROSS-CUTTING",
      "x": -1660,
      "y": 2560,
      "width": 3120,
      "height": 900,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "c_config",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`config.py`** 216 \u2014 every tunable\n\n34 getters, all env-driven with a working default,\nread on **each access** (never cached at import) and\nclamped at read time.\n\n**Stage toggles** `RESEARCH_FETCH` \u00b7 `RESEARCH_ANALYZE`\n**Retrieval** `FETCH_MAX_SOURCES=22` \u00b7 `FETCH_MAX_WORKERS=6`\n**Chunking** `CHUNK_TARGET_CHARS=1400` \u00b7 `CHUNKS_PER_SOURCE=6`\n**Extraction** `EXTRACT_BATCH_CHARS=13000` \u2190 *throughput dial*\n**Report** `REPORT_EVIDENCE_PER_SECTION=60` \u2190 *prompt-size dial*\n**Budgets** `RESEARCH_LLM_BUDGET=40` \u00b7 `RESEARCH_FETCH_BUDGET=28`",
      "x": -1620,
      "y": 2600,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 480,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "c_tests",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Tests \u2014 165 passing, 1 live**\n\n`test_llm.py` 589 \u2014 retry, fallback, the three\nrate-limit kinds, cooldowns, prompt ceilings,\n8-thread concurrency (8 callers \u2192 **1** attempt)\n\n`test_deep_research.py` 727 \u2014 fetch strategies,\nchunking, guards, stats accumulation, status\n\n`test_frontend_render.py` 125 \u2014 real `markdown.js`\nvia dukpy: citations, numbering, XSS\n\nRun: `pytest -q -m \"not live\"`",
      "x": -1000,
      "y": 2600,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 480
    },
    {
      "id": "c_legacy",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Off-path (dead but tested)**\n\n`backend/tools/` \u2014 `github.py` 117 \u00b7 `news.py` 107 \u00b7\n`serpapi.py` 98\n`backend/evidence/collector.py` 44\n\n**366 lines nothing on the live path imports.**\n`searcher.py` calls `serpapi.GoogleSearch` directly.\nKept alive only by 664 lines of tests\n(`test_github/news/serpapi/collector.py`) \u2014 roughly a\nthird of the codebase.",
      "x": -380,
      "y": 2600,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 480
    },
    {
      "id": "c_metrics",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Reference run, end to end**\n\nplan 1 \u2192 **7 searches** (4 sub-questions)\ncollect ~42 rows \u2192 **61 unique URLs**\nretrieve 61 \u2192 **25 fetched**, 64,796 words,\n  **135 chunks**, 6 references followed\nrelevance 135 \u2192 **70 kept**, diversified\nextract 70 \u2192 **110 verified findings**, 7 dimensions\nper-source synthesis \u2192 **9 assessed**\ncontradictions \u2192 **10**\nreport \u2192 **13,402 words**, 19 cited, 39 references",
      "x": 240,
      "y": 2600,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 480
    },
    {
      "id": "c_legend",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Legend**\n\n**Colours** \u2014 `6` interface \u00b7 `4` orchestration /\ncross-cutting \u00b7 `5` LLM + pipeline \u00b7\n`3` evidence \u00b7 `2` external I/O \u00b7 `1` output\n\n**Bold node title** \u2014 module or graph node\n`\u00b7  no LLM` \u2014 deterministic, costs no model call\n`\u00b7  LLM \u00d7N` \u2014 N model calls for that stage\n\n**Edge labels** \u2014 the data crossing that link.\nBidirectional pairs = request then response.\n\n**Read the flow left \u2192 right**: interface \u2192\norchestration \u2192 pipeline nodes \u2192 modules \u2192\nexternal \u2192 output. The bottom band is\ncross-cutting, not part of the runtime path.",
      "x": 860,
      "y": 2600,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 480
    },
    {
      "id": "m_planner2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`planner.py`** 280 \u00b7 1 LLM call\n\nPlan \u2192 dedupe \u2192 replace.\n\nTwo duplicate signals, own thresholds:\nrare-term (IDF) \u22650.70, char trigrams \u22650.45.\nReworded dup scores 0.61; distinct dims 0.05\u20130.09.\n\nOn any failure the surviving plan is used.",
      "x": 424,
      "y": 2190,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 260,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "m_throttle",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**`throttle.py`** 193\n\nProcess-wide pacing, one singleton per kind\n(`llm`, `search`) shared by every run.\n\n`per_minute` bounds the total in any window.\n`max_concurrent` stops two tabs jointly\nexceeding one quota. Verified exact spacing;\nslot released even when a call raises.\n\nDefault 12/min + 1 concurrent.",
      "x": 1112,
      "y": 1590,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "c_depth",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Depth, budget & pacing**\n\n`RESEARCH_MAX_ROUNDS` 2 \u00b7 ceiling 10\n`LLM_BUDGET` auto = 17 + 13/round\n`THROTTLE_LLM` 1 \u00b7 12/min \u00b7 1 concurrent\n\nCost for 43 calls: 30/min +1.4 min,\n20/min +2.1 min, 12/min +3.6 min.\n\nA starved budget logs a warning and the\nreport returns `partial`, never silently\ntruncated.",
      "x": -1620,
      "y": 3120,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "c_incr",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Incremental analysis**\n\n`ANALYSE_REUSE_SOURCES=1`\n\n`extracted_sources`: url \u2192 grade.\nA source is re-read only when its grade\n*improves* (snippet became a real document).\n\nPassages read, 10 docs +2/round:\nbefore 10\u219222\u219236\u219252, after 10\u219212\u219214\u219216",
      "x": -1000,
      "y": 3120,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "4"
    }
  ],
